# User interface texts: copyproject (first draft per docs/glossar-i18n.md; keys are never renamed)

copyproject-build-bauordner-laesst-sich-neu-erzeugen = build/ (build folder; can be created again)

copyproject-das-zeichen-c-ist-im-namen = The character “{ $c }” is not allowed in the name (/ \ : * ? " < > |).

copyproject-das-ziel-enthaelt-das-quellprojekt-waehle = The destination contains the source project. Choose another name or place.

copyproject-das-ziel-liegt-im-quellordner-des = The destination is inside the project's source folder. Choose another place.

copyproject-der-name-darf-nicht-mit-einem = The name must not start with a dot.

copyproject-der-name-darf-nicht-mit-punkt = The name must not end with a dot or a space (Windows).

copyproject-der-name-ist-leer = The name is empty.

copyproject-der-name-ist-zu-lang-hoechstens = The name is too long (100 characters at most).

copyproject-im-ordner-p1-liegt-keine-projektdatei = The folder { $p1 } has no project file (*.vcprj).

copyproject-n-ist-unter-windows-ein-reservierter = “{ $n }” is a reserved name on Windows.

copyproject-p1-gibt-es-schon-und-ist = “{ $p1 }” already exists and is not empty. Choose another name or place.

copyproject-p1-keine-gewoehnliche-datei = { $p1 } (not a regular file)

copyproject-p1-keine-gueltige-projektdatei-e = { $p1 }: not a valid project file ({ $e })

copyproject-p1-symbolische-verknuepfung = { $p1 } (symbolic link)

copyproject-versionsgeschichte-die-kopie-beginnt-ohne = version history; the copy starts without it
